# .gitleaksignore - Exclude test fixtures and mock data from Gitleaks secret scanning
#
# These are mock credentials used in unit tests and should not be flagged as security issues.
# Real credentials should NEVER be committed to this repository.
#
# Documentation: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks#gitleaksignore
#
# NOTE: .gitleaksignore uses exact fingerprints from findings, NOT glob patterns.
# Format: <file-path>:<rule-id>:<line-number>
# To add new exclusions, run Gitleaks and copy the "Fingerprint:" from the finding.

# Kubernetes test secrets (base64-encoded test credentials in testdata)
/repo/internal/controller/core/testdata/secrets/storageconfig-encoded-unmanaged.yaml:kubernetes-secret-yaml:2
/repo/internal/controller/testdata/secrets/dataconnection-encoded.yaml:kubernetes-secret-yaml:2

# Test private key in unit test
/repo/internal/controller/core/pod_controller_test.go:private-key:314

# Fake NVIDIA API key in mock
/repo/internal/controller/testdata/nvidia_api_mock.go:generic-api-key:36

# Note: This file should be reviewed regularly to ensure test data exclusions remain appropriate.
# Production code and configuration files are still scanned for secrets.
